### 🔴 Critical — Tests Giving False Confidence

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic — all 10 tests)

This suite is the textbook example of the anti-pattern you suspected. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called in declaration order, but **nothing meaningful is verified**. This is why bugs ship — the suite reaches 95% line coverage while proving almost nothing.

| Test Method (line) | Calls | Asserts | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (17) | `AddProduct` | ❌ None | No proof product was saved |
| `GetProduct_Works` (23) | `GetProduct` | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks SKU, Name, or Price |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (31) | `UpdatePrice` | ❌ None | Never verifies price changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (38) | `RemoveProduct` | ❌ None | Never verifies product is gone |
| `SearchProducts_Works` (45) | `Search` | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks results contain "Widget" |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` (54) | `GetAll` | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks count or contents |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (62) | `GetProductCount` | ❌ None | Discards the return value entirely |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (68) | `ApplyBulkDiscount` | ❌ None | Never verifies prices decreased |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` (76) | `ExportToCsv` | `IsNotNull` only | Never checks CSV content |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (84) | `ImportFromCsv` | ❌ None | Never verifies products were imported |

**5 tests have zero assertions.** The other 5 assert only `IsNotNull`, which passes for any non-null return — the method could return garbage and the test would pass.

